// The simulated dish of examples/cl_bridge (network.ent) on its own: a
// few seconds of it, quiet between bursts (a few a minute), under a spike
// a second a neuron. The same seed gives the same list of spikes (each one's step
// and channel, hashed in order) and the same checksum of every potential
// and weight, run again and on many threads; another seed another dish.
// RUN: %ent build %S/../../examples/cl_bridge/run.ent -o %t.one
// RUN: env ENT_PARALLEL_MIN=1 %ent build --parallel %S/../../examples/cl_bridge/run.ent -o %t.all
// RUN: %t.one 3 > %t.a
// RUN: %t.one 3 > %t.b
// RUN: env OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 %t.all 3 > %t.c
// RUN: %t.one 3 2 > %t.d
// RUN: diff %t.a %t.b
// RUN: diff %t.a %t.c
// RUN: not diff %t.a %t.d
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.a
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OTHER < %t.d
// A dish of 4096 neurons (wired through the grid of where they are):
// the same on many threads.
// RUN: %t.one 1 1 4096 > %t.e
// RUN: env OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 %t.all 1 1 4096 > %t.f
// RUN: diff %t.e %t.f
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BIG < %t.e

// CHECK: second 1: {{[0-4]}}.{{[0-9]+}} Hz a neuron
// CHECK: second 3: {{[0-4]}}.{{[0-9]+}} Hz a neuron
// CHECK: seed 1: 1024 neurons, 3000 steps, [[N:[0-9]+]] spikes
// CHECK: 44815 synapses, spikes heard [[HEARD:[0-9]+]], checksum [[SUM:[0-9]+]]
// OTHER: seed 2: 1024 neurons, 3000 steps
// OTHER: 44430 synapses
// BIG: seed 1: 4096 neurons, 1000 steps
// BIG: 243015 synapses
